  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Blue Dot Network development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Blue Dot Network is an initiative to create an internationally recognised certification framework for infrastructure projects that meet robust international standards for quality and sustainability, particularly in developing countries. The purpose of Blue Dot Network recognition is to assist countries in attracting private sector investment in projects that are environmentally and socially sustainable, resilient, open and transparent, and economically efficient. Australia has supported development of the Blue Dot Network since 2019, together with a range of partners.</narrative>
  </description>
